  "process_rubric": "# Process rubric: T4 (places similar to a given place)\n\nThe agent was given a query point, a month, k and a search box, and asked for the k most similar\nplaces by Clay embeddings, as `{\"chips\": [chips_id, ...]}` with the most similar first. The\nanswer can be found with one correct call of the `similar_places` tool. Judge **how faithfully**\nthe agent used the tool; the output metric scores the chip list. Score each item from 0 to 1 and\ncite the trace event IDs your score is based on.\n\n## planning\n\nDid the agent recognise that one embedding-similarity search with the given inputs answers the\ntask?\n\n- **1.0**: calls `similar_places` with the given point, year, month, k and search box (optionally\n  `embedding_at` first to look at the query chip), then answers.\n- **0.5**: gets there after unneeded detours (geocoding the given point, several exploratory\n  searches with other months or boxes).\n- **0.0**: never uses the embeddings tool.\n\n## tool_choice\n\nWere the arguments the ones the prompt gave?\n\n- **1.0**: lat/lon, year, month, k and search_bbox exactly as given.\n- **0.5**: one argument changed or missing (no search_bbox, a different k) without a reason.\n- **0.0**: arguments unrelated to the prompt (another place or month).\n\n## error_recovery\n\nWhen a call failed, did it react sensibly?\n\n- **1.0**: reads the error (e.g. \"month not staged\", \"no chip at this point\") and corrects the\n  call. Also 1.0 if no call failed.\n- **0.5**: retries the same failing call once or twice, then moves on.\n- **0.0**: loops on the failing call, or abandons the task.\n\n## honesty\n\nIs the answer faithful to the tool result?\n\n- **1.0**: returns exactly the chip IDs the tool returned, in its order, without the query chip.\n- **0.5**: real chip IDs, but reordered, truncated or mixed with results from another call\n  without saying so.\n- **0.0**: invents chip IDs, or returns coordinates or names instead of chip IDs.\n",
